# Exercise: Diminishing Returns
#
# Amdahl's Law predicts diminishing returns from adding workers.
#
# With p=0.75 (75% parallelizable):
#   1 worker:  speedup = 1.00x
#   2 workers: speedup = 1.60x  (+0.60)
#   4 workers: speedup = 2.29x  (+0.69)
#   8 workers: speedup = 2.91x  (+0.62)
#   infinity workers: speedup = 4.00x  (maximum!)
#
# Each additional worker helps less. This is why throwing
# more cores at a problem has limits.
#
# We demonstrate: 4 items, each 10ms, with serial overhead of 10ms.
# Total serial baseline = 10 + 40 = 50ms
# With 4 workers: 10 + 10 = 20ms (speedup ~ 2.5x, not 4x!)
#
# Your task: Run 4 items through 4 workers with serial overhead.
# Verify all items processed correctly.
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

# Helper: spawn a worker that processes one item
: spawn-one ( Channel Channel -- Channel Channel )
    2dup [ over chan.receive drop 10 time.sleep-ms 1 i.+ swap chan.send drop drop ] strand.spawn drop
    drop drop
;

: test-diminishing-returns ( -- )
    chan.make   # work
    chan.make   # results

    # Spawn 4 workers
    spawn-one
    spawn-one
    spawn-one
    spawn-one

    # Serial overhead: 10ms setup
    10 time.sleep-ms

    # Send 4 items
    over 10 swap chan.send drop
    over 20 swap chan.send drop
    over 30 swap chan.send drop
    over 40 swap chan.send drop

    # Your code here:
    # 1. Receive 4 results and sum them
    # 2. Serial overhead: 10ms aggregation
    # 3. Expected sum: 11 + 21 + 31 + 41 = 104
    drop drop 0

    # Do not edit below this line
    104 test.assert-eq
;
